# Installed by npm ci, from package-lock.json.
node_modules/

# Built by npm run build, and rebuilt by .github/workflows/pages.yml on every
# push. Nothing reads it that does not also build it.
dist/

# Types and settings Astro regenerates on every dev start and build.
.astro/

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deliberately NOT ignored, though it looks like build output:
#
#   public/data/          5.9 MB of quantised surfaces, cells and the manifest
#   src/content/generated.json
#
# Both are written by model/export_web.py, which needs likelihood.npz and the
# scraped GIFs -- around 210 MB of gitignored intermediates that CI does not
# have and should not rebuild. Tracking the exporter's output is what lets the
# Pages workflow build the site without any of them.
#
# The cost is that a research change does not reach the site until
# export_web.py is re-run and its output committed. check.py enforces this:
# "site, generated.json agrees with the data" fails whenever the JSON and the
# tracked CSVs disagree, so a stale export is a failing check rather than a
# quietly wrong page.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
